{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wm43hWmf17KYzHWDwQTkSU","type":"tool_result","content":"1836\t- **`doctor.sh` stopped discarding unsafe manifest records in silence** —\n1837\t  traversal, absolute path, any control byte, symlinked ancestor,\n1838\t  malformed digest and duplicate relpath are each a NAMED discard, capped\n1839\t  at 20 and folded into `UNRESOLVED` (rc 1); a manifest containing a NUL\n1840\t  is refused before the parse (`ba15c71`).\n1841\t- A fail-closed census of installer write sites\n1842\t  (`check-installer-write-safety.py`) ships as a RATCHET in `validate.yml`\n1843\t  with its blind spots declared in the plan, not papered over.\n1844\t\n1845\t### Changed — audit log resolves per PROJECT, not per `$HOME` (PLAN-182, ADR-001)\n1846\t\n1847\t**Adopter-visible if you run the framework in more than one repository\n1848\tunder the same `$HOME`.** Runtime state — the HMAC audit log, its key,\n1849\tlock, errors, salt and sidecars — now resolves through one family\n1850\tresolver (`.claude/hooks/_lib/runtime_paths.py`) using Claude Code's own\n1851\tpath-based project slug, instead of a literal `ceo-orchestration`\n1852\tdirectory shared by every project (`9de4efc`, `965fb13`, `3d16070`).\n1853\t\n1854\t- For repositories with DISTINCT resolved runtime directories, this separates\n1855\t  their chains and keys and provides correct"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c051953-0555-4b5d-b275-3a51ba918cc5","uuid":"ba909add-d1b5-4e57-99eb-6ed2f97e2c0b","timestamp":"2026-11-15T09:47:42.382Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"- **`doctor.sh` stopped discarding unsafe manifest records in silence** —\n  traversal, absolute path, any control byte, symlinked ancestor,\n  malformed digest and duplicate relpath are each a NAMED discard, capped\n  at 20 and folded into `UNRESOLVED` (rc 1)