{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JqzQKZc5v5ukqiv4qnRC5P","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Reflexion lessons — CRUD + relevance ranking.\n3\t\n4\tSprint 3 Item A. Implements Shinn et al. 2023 \"Reflexion\" pattern for\n5\tthe ceo-orchestration framework. When a benchmark scenario fails, the\n6\trunner writes a lesson file. When an agent is spawned, the top-3 most\n7\trelevant lessons are injected into the prompt.\n8\t\n9\t## Lesson storage\n10\t\n11\tEach lesson is a JSON file under:\n12\t\n13\t    $HOME/.claude/projects/<slug>/lessons/<lesson_id>.json\n14\t\n15\tLesson IDs are SHA-256 hashes of (scenario_id + created_at). Files are\n16\thuman-readable JSON, one per lesson.\n17\t\n18\t## Relevance ranking\n19\t\n20\t    score = archetype_match × scope_overlap × recency_decay\n21\t\n22\t- archetype_match: 1.0 if exact match, 0.3 if related, 0.0 otherwise\n23\t- scope_overlap: Jaccard similarity of lesson scope_tags vs task keywords\n24\t- recency_decay: exp(-days_since_lesson / 90) — 90-day e-folding time\n25\t  (half-life ≈ 62.4 days; PLAN-154 A14 docstring fix — the old\n26\t  \"90-day half-life\" wording overstated retention)\n27\t\n28\tTop 3 by score, capped at 2K total tokens of injected content.\n29\t\n30\t## PLAN-154 — gated learning loop (candidate lifecycle)\n31\t\n32\tDistiller-proposed lesson CANDIDATES live in a separate namespace,\n33\t``<lessons_dir>/candidates/<lesson_id>.json``, so no legacy reader\n34\t(``list_lessons`` / ``get_top_k`` / ``build_index`` / prune / ranker)\n35\tcan ever surface a non-approved candidate into a spawn prompt.\n36\t\n37\tState machine (zero self-activation — constraint 5):\n38\t\n39\t    add_candidate() ──> PENDING ──/lesson-review approve──> APPROVED\n40\t                          │  │\n41\t                          │  └──(TTL 30d)──> EXPIRED      (terminal)\n42\t                          └──(scan hit / scanner down /\n43\t                              tamper at approve)──> QUARANTINED (terminal)\n44\t\n45\t- The promotion boundary is fail-CLOSED (A4): injection-scanner\n46\t  unavailable OR scan hit at ``add_candidate`` → QUARANTINED.\n47\t- Approval events in the HMAC chain carry\n48\t  ``sha256(trigger + \"\\\\n\" + advisory_text)`` (A6). Renderers verify\n49\t  the recomputed hash against the chain BEFORE rendering; the chain —\n50\t  not this mutable ``$HOME`` store — is the integrity anchor.\n51\t- Every time function takes an injectable ``now_fn`` (A9); the wall\n52\t  clock is only the default.\n53\t- Candidate vocabulary is bounded (A5): advisory_text ≤ 200 chars, no\n54\t  backticks, no newlines, no control chars; trigger/scope_tags are\n55\t  closed-character-class tokens.\n56\t\n57\t## CLI\n58\t\n59\t    python3 lessons.py write --scenario-id X --archetype Y --remember \"...\" --scope \"tag1,tag2\" --agent-response \"...\" --expected \"...\"\n60\t    python3 lessons.py top3 --archetype Y --keywords \"tag1,tag2\"\n61\t    python3 lessons.py list\n62\t    python3 lessons.py prune --older-than-days 180\n63\t    # PLAN-154 candidate lifecycle:\n64\t    python3 lessons.py add-candidate --trigger t --text \"...\" --scope \"a,b\"\n65\t    python3 lessons.py candidates [--status PENDING] [--json]\n66\t    python3 lessons.py approve <lesson_id>\n67\t    python3 lessons.py expire-sweep\n68\t\n69\t## Constraints\n70\t\n71\t- stdlib-only, Python >= 3.9\n72\t- Directory scan capped at 1000 files (debate consensus R-DEV3)\n73\t- All agent_response content passes through _lib.redact before storage\n74\t\"\"\"\n75\t\n76\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n77\t\n78\timport hashlib\n79\timport json\n80\timport math\n81\timport os\n82\timport re\n83\timport sys\n84\timport time\n85\tfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\n86\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n87\tfrom pathlib import Path\n88\tfrom typing import Any, Callable, Dict, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n89\t\n90\t# Make _lib importable — lessons.py lives in .claude/scripts/,\n91\t# _lib lives in .claude/hooks/_lib/\n92\t_HOOKS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"hooks\"\n93\tif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n94\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n95\tfrom _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402  # PLAN-182 W1 single resolver\n96\t\n97\ttry:\n98\t    from _lib.redact import redact_secrets\n99\texcept ImportError:\n100\t    # Graceful degradation — if _lib isn't available, no-op redaction\n101\t    def redact_secrets(text: str) -> str:  # type: ignore[misc]\n102\t        return text\n103\t\n104\ttry:\n105\t    from _lib.filelock import FileLock, FileLockTimeout\n106\t    _FILELOCK_AVAILABLE = True\n107\texcept ImportError:\n108\t    _FILELOCK_AVAILABLE = False\n109\t\n110\ttry:\n111\t    from _lib.audit_emit import emit_lesson_write as _emit_lesson_write\n112\t    from _lib.audit_emit import emit_lesson_read as _emit_lesson_read\n113\t    _AUDIT_EMIT_AVAILABLE = True\n114\texcept ImportError:\n115\t    _AUDIT_EMIT_AVAILABLE = False\n116\t\n117\t\n118\t# Maximum lesson files to scan per query (debate consensus R-DEV3)\n119\t_MAX_SCAN = 1000\n120\t\n121\t# Maximum total tokens of injected lesson content\n122\t_MAX_INJECT_TOKENS = 2000\n123\t\n124\t# Approximate chars per token for budget estimation\n125\t_CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 4\n126\t\n127\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n128\t# PLAN-154 — candidate lifecycle constants (constraints 3/5, A5/A9)\n129\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n130\t\n131\t# Candidate states. QUARANTINED and EXPIRED are TERMINAL — no transition\n132\t# ever leaves them (A4/A9). APPROVED is reached ONLY via approve_candidate\n133\t# (the /lesson-review human gate); nothing self-activates.\n134\tSTATUS_PENDING = \"PENDING\"\n135\tSTATUS_APPROVED = \"APPROVED\"\n136\tSTATUS_QUARANTINED = \"QUARANTINED\"\n137\tSTATUS_EXPIRED = \"EXPIRED\"\n138\tCANDIDATE_STATUSES = frozenset(\n139\t    {STATUS_PENDING, STATUS_APPROVED, STATUS_QUARANTINED, STATUS_EXPIRED}\n140\t)\n141\tTERMINAL_STATUSES = frozenset({STATUS_QUARANTINED, STATUS_EXPIRED})\n142\t\n143\t# TTL for PENDING candidates (constraint 5). Expiry is STRICT: a\n144\t# candidate expires when age > TTL (exactly-at-TTL is NOT expired —\n145\t# golden-value boundary tests pin TTL±1s). The 7-day warning window is\n146\t# COUNT-ONLY data; no candidate text ever travels through it (A9).\n147\tCANDIDATE_TTL_DAYS = 30\n148\tCANDIDATE_WARN_DAYS = 7\n149\t\n150\t# Bounded candidate vocabulary (A5). advisory_text: length-capped,\n151\t# backtick-free, newline-free, control-char-free. trigger + scope tags:\n152\t# closed-character-class tokens (injection-inert by construction).\n153\tfrom _lib._lessons_parts.config import CANDIDATE_TEXT_MAX_CHARS\n154\t_CANDIDATE_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{0,63}$\")\n155\t_MAX_CANDIDATE_TAGS = 16\n156\t\n157\t# Bounded HMAC-chain scan (A6 verify-before-render). The chain rotates at\n158\t# 10 MiB per file (audit_rotation.py); we scan the current file plus the\n159\t# most recent rotated siblings, newest first, under a total byte budget.\n160\t_CHAIN_SCAN_MAX_FILES = 4\n161\t_CHAIN_SCAN_MAX_BYTES = 48 * 1024 * 1024\n162\t\n163\t# Audit actions emitted by the candidate lifecycle. Registration in\n164\t# audit_emit._KNOWN_ACTIONS is integrator-owned (4-file coupling);\n165\t# pre-registration, emit_generic() is a schema-compliant no-op.\n166\t_ACTION_CANDIDATE_WRITTEN = \"lesson_candidate_written\"\n167\t_ACTION_APPROVED = \"lesson_approved\"\n168\t_ACTION_QUARANTINED = \"lesson_quarantined\"\n169\t_ACTION_EXPIRED = \"lesson_expired\"\n170\t_ACTION_INTEGRITY_FLAG = \"lesson_integrity_flag\"\n171\t\n172\t\n173\t@dataclass\n174\tclass Lesson:\n175\t    \"\"\"A single reflexion lesson.\n176\t\n177\t    PLAN-006 Phase 4 (ADR-015): extended with `hit_count` / `miss_count`\n178\t    for outcome tracking. Absence (or zero) = untested; populated via\n179\t    `record_outcome()` when a benchmark run applies this lesson.\n180\t    \"\"\"\n181\t\n182\t    lesson_id: str = \"\"\n183\t    created_at: str = \"\"  # ISO 8601\n184\t    scenario_id: str = \"\"\n185\t    archetype: str = \"\"\n186\t    remember_this: str = \"\"  # ≤ 200 chars\n187\t    scope_tags: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n188\t    agent_response: str = \"\"  # redacted before storage\n189\t    expected_response: str = \"\"\n190\t    # Outcome loop (ADR-015)\n191\t    hit_count: int = 0\n192\t    miss_count: int = 0\n193\t    last_outcome_at: str = \"\"  # ISO 8601 of most recent hit/miss\n194\t\n195\t    def hit_rate(self) -> Optional[float]:\n196\t        \"\"\"Ratio hits / (hits + misses). None when n < 3 (low signal).\"\"\"\n197\t        n = self.hit_count + self.miss_count\n198\t        if n < 3:\n199\t            return None\n200\t        return self.hit_count / n\n201\t\n202\t\n203\t# Bind declarations to this facade so runtime lookups honor monkeypatches.\n204\tfrom _lib._audit_emit_parts import install as _install_lessons_parts\n205\t_install_lessons_parts(globals(), (\"storage_audit\", \"lessons\", \"candidates\", \"render\", \"cli\"),\n206\t                       package=\"_lib._lessons_parts\")\n207\tdel _install_lessons_parts\n208\tif not __annotations__:\n209\t    del __annotations__\n210\t\n211\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n212\t    sys.exit(main())\n213\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c051953-0555-4b5d-b275-3a51ba918cc5","uuid":"21422b77-66b8-49ce-8b66-8a20ffc8f99b","timestamp":"2026-11-15T09:47:58.931Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/.claude/scripts/lessons.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Reflexion lessons — CRUD + relevance ranking.\n\nSprint 3 Item A. Implements Shinn et al. 2023 \"Reflexion\" pattern for\nthe ceo-orchestration framework. When a benchmark scenario fails, the\nrunner writes a lesson file. When an agent is spawned, the top-3 most\nrelevant lessons are injected into the prompt.\n\n## Lesson storage\n\nEach lesson is a JSON file under:\n\n    $HOME/.claude/projects/<slug>/lessons/<lesson_id>.json\n\nLesson IDs are SHA-256 hashes of (scenario_id + created_at). Files are\nhuman-readable JSON, one per lesson.\n\n## Relevance ranking\n\n    score = archetype_match × scope_overlap × recency_decay\n\n- archetype_match: 1.0 if exact match, 0.3 if related, 0.0 otherwise\n- scope_overlap: Jaccard similarity of lesson scope_tags vs task keywords\n- recency_decay: exp(-days_since_lesson / 90) — 90-day e-folding time\n  (half-life ≈ 62.4 days; PLAN-154 A14 docstring fix — the old\n  \"90-day half-life\" wording overstated retention)\n\nTop 3 by score, capped at 2K total tokens of injected content.\n\n## PLAN-154 — gated learning loop (candidate lifecycle)\n\nDistiller-proposed lesson CANDIDATES live in a separate namespace,\n``<lessons_dir>/candidates/<lesson_id>.json``, so no legacy reader\n(``list_lessons`` / ``get_top_k`` / ``build_index`` / prune / ranker)\ncan ever surface a non-approved candidate into a spawn prompt.\n\nState machine (zero self-activation — constraint 5):\n\n    add_candidate() ──> PENDING ──/lesson-review approve──> APPROVED\n                          │  │\n                          │  └──(TTL 30d)──> EXPIRED      (terminal)\n                          └──(scan hit / scanner down /\n                              tamper at approve)──> QUARANTINED (terminal)\n\n- The promotion boundary is fail-CLOSED (A4): injection-scanner\n  unavailable OR scan hit at ``add_candidate`` → QUARANTINED.\n- Approval events in the HMAC chain carry\n  ``sha256(trigger + \"\\\\n\" + advisory_text)`` (A6). Renderers verify\n  the recomputed hash against the chain BEFORE rendering; the chain —\n  not this mutable ``$HOME`` store — is the integrity anchor.\n- Every time function takes an injectable ``now_fn`` (A9); the wall\n  clock is only the default.\n- Candidate vocabulary is bounded (A5): advisory_text ≤ 200 chars, no\n  backticks, no newlines, no control chars; trigger/scope_tags are\n  closed-character-class tokens.\n\n## CLI\n\n    python3 lessons.py write --scenario-id X --archetype Y --remember \"...\" --scope \"tag1,tag2\" --agent-response \"...\" --expected \"...\"\n    python3 lessons.py top3 --archetype Y --keywords \"tag1,tag2\"\n    python3 lessons.py list\n    python3 lessons.py prune --older-than-days 180\n    # PLAN-154 candidate lifecycle:\n    python3 lessons.py add-candidate --trigger t --text \"...\" --scope \"a,b\"\n    python3 lessons.py candidates [--status PENDING] [--json]\n    python3 lessons.py approve <lesson_id>\n    python3 lessons.py expire-sweep\n\n## Constraints\n\n- stdlib-only, Python >= 3.9\n- Directory scan capped at 1000 files (debate consensus R-DEV3)\n- All agent_response content passes through _lib.redact before storage\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, Dict, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n\n# Make _lib importable — lessons.py lives in .claude/scripts/,\n# _lib lives in .claude/hooks/_lib/\n_HOOKS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"hooks\"\nif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\nfrom _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402  # PLAN-182 W1 single resolver\n\ntry:\n    from _lib.redact import redact_secrets\nexcept ImportError:\n    # Graceful degradation — if _lib isn't available, no-op redaction\n    def redact_secrets(text: str) -> str:  # type: ignore[misc]\n        return text\n\ntry:\n    from _lib.filelock import FileLock, FileLockTimeout\n    _FILELOCK_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    _FILELOCK_AVAILABLE = False\n\ntry:\n    from _lib.audit_emit import emit_lesson_write as _emit_lesson_write\n    from _lib.audit_emit import emit_lesson_read as _emit_lesson_read\n    _AUDIT_EMIT_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    _AUDIT_EMIT_AVAILABLE = False\n\n\n# Maximum lesson files to scan per query (debate consensus R-DEV3)\n_MAX_SCAN = 1000\n\n# Maximum total tokens of injected lesson content\n_MAX_INJECT_TOKENS = 2000\n\n# Approximate chars per token for budget estimation\n_CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 4\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PLAN-154 — candidate lifecycle constants (constraints 3/5, A5/A9)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n# Candidate states. QUARANTINED and EXPIRED are TERMINAL — no transition\n# ever leaves them (A4/A9). APPROVED is reached ONLY via approve_candidate\n# (the /lesson-review human gate); nothing self-activates.\nSTATUS_PENDING = \"PENDING\"\nSTATUS_APPROVED = \"APPROVED\"\nSTATUS_QUARANTINED = \"QUARANTINED\"\nSTATUS_EXPIRED = \"EXPIRED\"\nCANDIDATE_STATUSES = frozenset(\n    {STATUS_PENDING, STATUS_APPROVED, STATUS_QUARANTINED, STATUS_EXPIRED}\n)\nTERMINAL_STATUSES = frozenset({STATUS_QUARANTINED, STATUS_EXPIRED})\n\n# TTL for PENDING candidates (constraint 5). Expiry is STRICT: a\n# candidate expires when age > TTL (exactly-at-TTL is NOT expired —\n# golden-value boundary tests pin TTL±1s). The 7-day warning window is\n# COUNT-ONLY data; no candidate text ever travels through it (A9).\nCANDIDATE_TTL_DAYS = 30\nCANDIDATE_WARN_DAYS = 7\n\n# Bounded candidate vocabulary (A5). advisory_text: length-capped,\n# backtick-free, newline-free, control-char-free. trigger + scope tags:\n# closed-character-class tokens (injection-inert by construction).\nfrom _lib._lessons_parts.config import CANDIDATE_TEXT_MAX_CHARS\n_CANDIDATE_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{0,63}$\")\n_MAX_CANDIDATE_TAGS = 16\n\n# Bounded HMAC-chain scan (A6 verify-before-render). The chain rotates at\n# 10 MiB per file (audit_rotation.py); we scan the current file plus the\n# most recent rotated siblings, newest first, under a total byte budget.\n_CHAIN_SCAN_MAX_FILES = 4\n_CHAIN_SCAN_MAX_BYTES = 48 * 1024 * 1024\n\n# Audit actions emitted by the candidate lifecycle. Registration in\n# audit_emit._KNOWN_ACTIONS is integrator-owned (4-file coupling);\n# pre-registration, emit_generic() is a schema-compliant no-op.\n_ACTION_CANDIDATE_WRITTEN = \"lesson_candidate_written\"\n_ACTION_APPROVED = \"lesson_approved\"\n_ACTION_QUARANTINED = \"lesson_quarantined\"\n_ACTION_EXPIRED = \"lesson_expired\"\n_ACTION_INTEGRITY_FLAG = \"lesson_integrity_flag\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Lesson:\n    \"\"\"A single reflexion lesson.\n\n    PLAN-006 Phase 4 (ADR-015): extended with `hit_count` / `miss_count`\n    for outcome tracking. Absence (or zero) = untested; populated via\n    `record_outcome()` when a benchmark run applies this lesson.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    lesson_id: str = \"\"\n    created_at: str = \"\"  # ISO 8601\n    scenario_id: str = \"\"\n    archetype: str = \"\"\n    remember_this: str = \"\"  # ≤ 200 chars\n    scope_tags: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    agent_response: str = \"\"  # redacted before storage\n    expected_response: str = \"\"\n    # Outcome loop (ADR-015)\n    hit_count: int = 0\n    miss_count: int = 0\n    last_outcome_at: str = \"\"  # ISO 8601 of most recent hit/miss\n\n    def hit_rate(self) -> Optional[float]:\n        \"\"\"Ratio hits / (hits + misses). None when n < 3 (low signal).\"\"\"\n        n = self.hit_count + self.miss_count\n        if n < 3:\n            return None\n        return self.hit_count / n\n\n\n# Bind declarations to this facade so runtime lookups honor monkeypatches.\nfrom _lib._audit_emit_parts import install as _install_lessons_parts\n_install_lessons_parts(globals(), (\"storage_audit\", \"lessons\", \"candidates\", \"render\", \"cli\"),\n                       package=\"_lib._lessons_parts\")\ndel _install_lessons_parts\nif not __annotations__:\n    del __annotations__\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":213,"startLine":1,"totalLines":213}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JqzQKZc5v5ukqiv4qnRC5P","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
