ep is that set's\n      # readout — one line per PR, so the debt is visible while OQ-1 is open.\n      # `continue-on-error: true` makes it structurally incapable of blocking\n      # a merge. Output is BOUNDED on purpose: `--strict` lists every site\n      # (424 lines today), which is a wall nobody reads, so only the summary\n      # line and a short tail are printed. The rc is captured immediately and\n      # printed rather than swallowed — `cmd > log; RC=$?` and never\n      # `cmd || true`, which would report success for every outcome.\n      - name: check-installer-write-safety.py --strict (advisory, OQ-1)\n        continue-on-error: true\n        run: |\n          set -uo pipefail\n          LOG=\"${RUNNER_TEMP:-/tmp}/iws-strict.log\"\n          python3 .claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py --strict > \"$LOG\" 2>&1\n          RC=$?\n          echo \"--strict rc=$RC — ADVISORY; OQ-1 decides when (and whether) this becomes a gate.\"\n          grep -E '^--strict: ' \"$LOG\" || echo \"(no --strict summary line — see the tail below)\"\n          tail -n 15 \"$LOG\"\n\n      # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n      # Step: Python toolchain for the steps below (Sprint 2 A.4)\n      # PLAN-186 W4a deleted the hook/script unit-test steps this banner\n      # used to introduce; `hook-tests-python-matrix` runs those suites\n      # now, in 3.9 AND 3.12. What stays is the toolchain later steps of\n      # this job still use — MEASURED, not assumed: TWO of them INVOKE\n      # pytest (the PLAN-155 Wave 6 teeth and the PLAN-152 tests-01\n      # roots); the npm packlist gate uses the selected python3","numLines":40,"startLine":405,"totalLines":1787}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019q77arvWWfAi6mBXwd7x2J","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
