{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VJjfzneiKaPbq7SyDmVN8i","type":"tool_result","content":".claude/hooks/check_arbitration_kernel.py:271:    # marker's prev_value is restored into it by night-mode off —\n.claude/hooks/check_arbitration_kernel.py:273:    # (night-mode.py writes them as a process), so they sit at kernel\n.claude/hooks/check_arbitration_kernel.py:278:    \".claude/state/night-mode.json\",\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:41:    land below the glob literal floor: `python3 .claude/scripts/$'night-mode.py'`\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:134:# bug. The `!` rail and the `night-mode` name stay in the base message, so the\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:146:# answer: without it the message quotes `.claude/scripts/night-mode.p{y..y}`,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:189:        \"GOVERNANCE: this bash command INVOKES the night-mode posture toggle \"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:193:        \"`!` prefix (`! python3 .claude/scripts/night-mode.py on|off|status`) \"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:210:        f\"night-mode posture toggle ({spelled!r}). A link is a second live \"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:217:        \"(`! python3 .claude/scripts/night-mode.py on|off|status`). Copying \"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:306:        # confusing night-mode reason.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:336:                             # path (`S=.claude/scripts/night-mode.py; …`). shlex\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:426:            return _e4_deny_reason(tok, expansion_pass)  # direct exec: `./…/night-mode.py on`\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_scan.py:430:            # `$(echo …/night-mode.py) on` — substitution IN COMMAND POSITION.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:296:#     python3 .claude/scripts/night-mode.py on\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:297:#     ./.claude/scripts/night-mode.py on\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:300:# `_CANONICAL_GUARDS` note, settings.json's `_night_mode_deny_surface_comment`,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:324:#   • `night-mode.py`'s own SELF-PATH GUARD → execution through an alias that\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:350:# recognised only SPELLINGS, so `ln -s .claude/scripts/night-mode.py /tmp/nm &&\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:356:# (`cp …/night-mode.py .claude/scripts/nm2.py && python3 .claude/scripts/nm2.py\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:364:#   • IN THE SCRIPT — `night-mode.py` refuses to run unless the file it was\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:365:#     invoked as IS the canonical `<repo>/.claude/scripts/night-mode.py`. That\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:376:_E4_POSTURE_TOGGLE_SCRIPTS = frozenset({\".claude/scripts/night-mode.py\"})\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:413:#   python3 .claude/scripts/{night-mode,other}.py on   -> 2 words, argv[1] is the toggle\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:414:#   python3 .claude/scripts/night-mode{,}.py on        -> 2 identical words\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:416:#   python3 .claude/scripts/night-mode.p{y..y} on      -> ONE word: the canonical path\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:421:# (`TOGGLE RAN argv=['.claude/scripts/night-mode.py', 'on']`). There is no\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:427:# globbing it applies here, and more sharply: replacing `{night-mode,other}`\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:511:#     env  -u FOO  python3 .claude/scripts/night-mode.py on\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_p