{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KJqyXcLtLz2nPGUzVgv5Lp","type":"tool_result","content":"255\t    \".github/workflows/actionlint.yml\",\n256\t    # PLAN-089 Wave A.4 — ADR-116-AMEND-1 kernel-extension-v2 END\n257\t    # PLAN-099 Wave E.1 — ADR-129 / ADR-135 federation paths (6 entries).\n258\t    # Federation enable + LAN sentinel pairs + peer registry must be\n259\t    # kernel-guarded so a sub-agent cannot forge an enable / bypass\n260\t    # the LAN gate by overwriting peers.yaml. The trailing glob covers\n261\t    # the dir-root semantic (plan §3 Wave E.1 entry #1) — any future\n262\t    # file added under .claude/data/federation/ inherits kernel-guard.\n263\t    \".claude/data/federation/peers.yaml\",\n264\t    \".claude/data/federation/enabled.md\",\n265\t    \".claude/data/federation/enabled.md.asc\",\n266\t    \".claude/data/federation/lan-enabled.md\",\n267\t    \".claude/data/federation/lan-enabled.md.asc\",\n268\t    \".claude/data/federation/**/*\",\n269\t    # PLAN-165 p1-corrected (NM-01/CX-1): machine-local posture STATE.\n270\t    # The overlay decides the NEXT session's permission mode and the\n271\t    # marker's prev_value is restored into it by night-mode off —\n272\t    # posture-write by proxy. No ceremony ever tool-edits these\n273\t    # (night-mode.py writes them as a process), so they sit at kernel\n274\t    # tier: no sentinel can grant a tool write. The WRITER script is\n275\t    # deliberately canonical-tier only (future ceremonies must be able\n276\t    # to evolve it under sentinel).\n277\t    \".claude/settings.local.json\",\n278\t    \".claude/state/night-mode.json\",\n279\t    # PLAN162_FIX_3 (PLAN-162 findings #3 + #8, consensus C10) — the two\n280\t    # files the guards themselves TRUST, previously guarded by NEITHER\n281\t    # rail (verified on HEAD: canonical=False, kernel=False for both):\n282\t    #\n283\t    #   1. the ADR-121 sentinel signer REGISTRY — the identity root\n284\t    #